review_comments.body:
I think this has potential alignment issues that didn't exist previously. For example, on 32-bit platforms `allocated` will be four bytes. If the array stores doubles, they will be aligned to 4 bytes instead of the required 8 bytes.

I think we need an `_Alignas()` for items. Something like:

```
typedef struct {
    Py_ssize_t allocated;
    _Alignas(8) char items[];
} arraydata;
```

